* Behavioural models for the battery-input simulations.
* The LCSC parts on the board have no vendor SPICE models; these are
* fitted to the datasheet headline numbers and are good for trends,
* not exact values.

* Q1 SP40P04NK: -40 V P-MOSFET, RDS(on) 4.9 mOhm @ -10 V, Vth -1.7 V,
* Ciss 6.5 nF, Crss 0.44 nF. VDMOS includes the body diode.
.model SP40P04NK VDMOS pchan Vto=-1.7 Kp=60 Rd=1.5m Rs=1m Rg=2
+ Cgs=6n Cgdmax=1.5n Cgdmin=0.3n Cjo=1.5n Is=1e-11 N=1.1 Rb=3m BV=40

* D2 BZT52C15 15 V zener (Zzt about 30 ohm at 5 mA)
.model BZT52C15 D(Is=1e-14 Rs=8 BV=15 IBV=5m Cjo=40p)

* SMCJ18A unidirectional TVS (D1, D3): VBR 20.0-22.1 V,
* VC 29.2 V at IPP 51.4 A, about 3 nF at 0 V.
.subckt SMCJ18A A K
Dfwd A K DTVSF
Rz K n1 0.16
Dz A n1 DTVSZ
.model DTVSF D(Is=1e-10 N=1.6 Rs=4m Cjo=3n)
.model DTVSZ D(Is=1e-14 Rs=1m BV=20.8 IBV=1m)
.ends

* SMBJ18CA bidirectional TVS (D10): VBR 20.0-22.1 V, VC 29.2 V at 20.5 A
.subckt SMBJ18CA A K
Rz1 A n1 0.2
D1 n1 m DTVSB
D2 K m DTVSB
Rm m A 100Meg
.model DTVSB D(Is=1e-14 Rs=0.2 BV=20.8 IBV=1m Cjo=1.2n)
.ends

* RoboClaw reverse path: H-bridge body diodes, PGND -> motor pin -> BAT+
* (two diodes in series per leg, two legs per channel, two channels).
.subckt RC_BODY BATP BATM
D1 BATM n1 DBODY
D2 n1 BATP DBODY
.model DBODY D(Is=1e-9 N=1.3 Rs=2.5m)
.ends

* rshunt (1 Gohm from every node to ground) stops the floating TVS midpoints
* from stalling the solver; it has no visible effect on the results.
.options method=gear rshunt=1e9
.model SWM SW(Ron=1m Roff=10Meg Vt=0.5 Vh=0.1)
